{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory (`cards/sos/sos_<N>/`) contains a `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a `card_impl.py` template (stub class) to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples, refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for rules, and read engine source modules for API discovery. The user explicitly states: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card mechanics: Converge, Casualty, Affinity, Paradigm, Miracle, Prepared (MDFC), Surveil, Counter spells, Planeswalker loyalty abilities, coin flips, cost reduction, attack triggers, token creation, reanimation, skip-turns\n   - Engine architecture: CardImpl hook methods, event-driven triggers (TriggerManager/fire_event), replacement effects (ReplacementManager), continuous effects (7-layer system, EffectManager), stack/priority loop, mana pool with color tracking, state-based actions\n   - Testing: DeterministicPlayer with scripted choices, test_utils (create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers)\n   - Python: dataclasses, Flag enums (Keyword), frozen dataclasses (ManaCost, HybridManaSymbol)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md` — Hard rules: card location invariant; engine_tests read-only; do NOT modify `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`; own SOS tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`; additive-only engine modifications (may add/modify bodies, must NOT rename/move/delete existing engine items).\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — CardImpl base with hooks: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`. Creature(base_power, base_toughness, power/toughness properties incl counters, _reset_characteristics). Planeswalker(starting_loyalty, loyalty, get_loyalty_abilities). Land(can_cast=False, get_mana_abilities).\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` and `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` are DEFINED but NOT FIRED anywhere. MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent has `destination`, `prevented` fields.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — `cast_spell(game, player, card)` pipeline; sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (a LIST). `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts without mana. `get_cost_reduction()` only calls `card.cost_reduction(game)`. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/stack.py` — `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` for spell copies (casualty). StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability). priority_loop().\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step` sets is_attacking=True, taps unless VIGILANCE, but does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent. _can_attack, _can_block, _deal_damage.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — helpers: deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card, discard, create_token, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap. draw_card tracks `cards_drawn_this_turn`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` fired with NO player arg (use game.active_player in condition). Untap clears summoning_sick, resets land_plays_remaining=1.\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` — ManaPool with last_payment_colors property (distinct Colors, excludes colorless). _MANA_TO_COLOR mapping.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_205/card_impl.py` (WardensOfTheCycle) — converge: `self.colors_spent: int = 0` default, on_resolve does `for _ in range(self.colors_spent)`. Tests set colors_spent as INT directly, but pipeline sets LIST — inconsistency to handle.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_134/card_impl.py` (Ajani) & `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py` (Kaito) — Planeswalker pattern: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1, effect=_fn, description=...)]`; uses `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)`; register_triggers for passives.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_244/card_impl.py` (Progenitus) — register_replacement_effects pattern with ReplacementEffect(event_type=MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent), condition checks `event.card is source`, sets `event.prevented=True`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` — Stub classes confirm class names/signatures: TheDawningArchaic, TogetherAsOne, EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares, ManaSculpt, RalZarekGuestLecturer (Planeswalker, Ral, loyalty 3), etc.\n   - `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py` — READ-ONLY reference; shows existing cast_spell behavior tests I must not break (timing, mana payment, hooks, LIFO stack). Confirms `test_cast_with_targets_passes_to_stack_object`.\n   - SOS card_impl.py stubs (all 10) — each currently just `class XxxYyy(CardImpl): pass` — must be filled in.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None yet — still in exploration/reading phase, no code written or executed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Identified that SpellCastTriggeredEvent and AttacksTriggeredEvent are defined but never fired — I will need to add firing to cast_spell and declare_attackers_step respectively. Identified converge colors_spent type inconsistency (list in pipeline vs int in tests) — plan to handle both. Planned engine extensions: counter_spell helper, surveil helper, granted-affinity cost reduction hook, alternative-cost casting for miracle/paradigm.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - (System reminders about deferred tools, skills, and task tracking reminders — not direct user requests)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - #1 [in_progress] Explore FDN reference cards for mechanic patterns\n   - #2 Implement sos_226 Silverquill (casualty) — medium, good starting point\n   - #3 Implement sos_57 Mana Sculpt (counter) — medium\n   - #4 Implement sos_4 Together as One (converge) — complex\n   - #5 Implement sos_1 The Dawning Archaic — complex\n   - #6 Implement sos_245 Witherbloom (affinity) — complex\n   - #7 Implement sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex — complex\n   - #8 Implement sos_13 Emeritus of Truce (prepared/MDFC) — complex\n   - #9 Implement sos_120 Improvisation Capstone (paradigm) — complex\n   - #10 Implement sos_201 Lorehold (miracle) — expert\n   - #11 Implement sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker — expert\n   - #12 Write tests and run full suite\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was completing the exploration phase (task #1). I had just read `engine_tests/test_casting.py` (to understand existing cast_spell test behavior I must preserve when I add SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing) and the partial `cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` (which confirmed all 10 SOS card class names and base types/signatures). The exploration is essentially complete — I have read all core engine modules, all 10 SOS specs, and all relevant FDN reference examples. No card implementations or engine edits have been made yet. The plan was to start implementing cards in order of complexity (easiest first: Silverquill/Mana Sculpt), building engine infrastructure as needed (firing SpellCastTriggeredEvent and AttacksTriggeredEvent, counter_spell helper, surveil helper, granted-affinity cost reduction, alternative-cost casting).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Mark task #1 (exploration) complete and begin implementing the first card. Per my established plan and task ordering, start with the lowest-complexity card to establish patterns: sos_226 Silverquill (casualty, medium tier) or sos_57 Mana Sculpt (counter, medium tier). For Silverquill, this requires first adding `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` firing in `engine/casting.py` `cast_spell()` (which I confirmed is currently never fired), then implementing the casualty static ability via a SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger that offers to sacrifice a creature with power≥1 and uses `copy_spell()` to copy the instant/sorcery spell. This is directly in line with the user's explicit request to \"make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics\" and the pending implementation tasks. Before any engine modification to cast_spell, ensure the changes preserve all behaviors verified in `engine_tests/test_casting.py` (timing, mana payment, hooks, LIFO ordering, target passing).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6","uuid":"cf517a56-b861-4e48-a8d3-c641730a73da","timestamp":"2026-05-30T04:07:52.199Z","isSynthetic":true}
