{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory (`cards/sos/sos_<N>/`) contains a `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a `card_impl.py` template (stub class) to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples, refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for rules, and read engine source modules for API discovery. The user explicitly states: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n   Tests for an SOS card go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (I create these). Do NOT modify `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`. Engine modifications must be additive (may add/modify bodies; must NOT rename/move/delete existing engine items).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics to implement: Casualty (Silverquill), Counter (Mana Sculpt), Converge (Together as One), graveyard-cost-reduction + attack-cast-from-graveyard (Dawning Archaic), Affinity for creatures granter (Witherbloom), land→creature + mana abilities (Great Hall), Prepared/MDFC (Emeritus // Swords to Plowshares), Paradigm (Improvisation Capstone), Miracle granter + loot (Lorehold), Planeswalker with Surveil/discard/reanimate/coin-flip-skip-turns (Ral Zarek).\n   - Engine architecture: CardImpl hooks; event-driven TriggerManager (condition `(game,event)->bool`, effect `(game)->None` — effect does NOT receive event, captures via closure); ReplacementManager (\"instead\" semantics, applied inline); 7-layer EffectManager; LIFO stack + priority_loop; ManaPool with last_payment_colors; state-based actions; APNAP trigger ordering.\n   - Testing: DeterministicPlayer scripted choices (deque popped by choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order); test_utils helpers.\n   - Python: dataclasses, Flag enums (Keyword), frozen ManaCost/HybridManaSymbol.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/run_manifest.json` — card_filter [1,4,13,57,97,120,201,226,245,257], benchmark_set \"sos\".\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` — rules; FDN cards with tests.py: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244. Bare package imports (workspace root on sys.path).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — `cast_spell(game,player,card)`: timing→can_cast→hand→move to stack→clear stale colors_spent→targets+filter+protection→cost_reduction→pay→`card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`→on_cast→push StackObject. Does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent (I must add). `cast_spell_free(game,player,card,from_zone)`. `_resolve_spell`: sets card.chosen_targets, calls on_resolve, then `move_to_zone(...STACK, BATTLEFIELD)` for permanents else `(...STACK, GRAVEYARD)` with NO replacement_event. `get_cost_reduction` only calls `card.cost_reduction(game)` (single-card self-reduction, clamped to generic). Planned edit: in `_resolve_spell` else-branch use `dest = Zone.EXILE if getattr(card,\"_exile_on_graveyard\",False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/stack.py` — StackObject(source, controller, targets=[], on_resolve, is_mana_ability). `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` shallow-copies source card, on_resolve calls copied_card.on_resolve directly. priority_loop resolves top when both pass.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller) and AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker) DEFINED but NOT FIRED. MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented; card→None) + subclasses CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(creature), PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(permanent), SacrificeReplacementEvent(permanent). BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent() no fields.\n   - `/workspace/engine/triggers.py` — fire_event collects matching by isinstance + condition, pushes StackObject(source=trigger.source, controller=trigger.controller, on_resolve=trigger.effect) in APNAP order. Effect gets only game.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — full class hierarchy; hooks listed in analysis; LoyaltyAbility/ActivatedAbility/ManaAbility/Mode dataclasses.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step`: eligible = creatures with base_power and _can_attack; active.choose(eligible,\"declare attackers\"); sets attacker.is_attacking=True, taps unless VIGILANCE. Does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (I must add per-attacker, set both attacker & creature).\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — helpers create_token (is_token=True, fires ETB then registers), sacrifice/destroy (use move_to_zone with replacement events), add_counter (handles \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\", generic dict), draw_card (tracks cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent), exile, discard.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py` — `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`: replacement applied only `if replacement_event is not None and leaving_battlefield`. Planned edit: change to `if replacement_event is not None:` (existing callers always leave battlefield, so no behavior change). move_zone deletes obj.colors_spent on zone change. _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP maps \"graveyard/exile/hand/library\".\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` — last_payment_colors = distinct non-colorless Colors of last pay(), sorted. No \"amount of mana spent\" tracked (Mana Sculpt may need card.mana_cost.cmc or a new card.mana_spent attribute set in cast_spell).\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` at upkeep; NO main-phase event exists (Mana Sculpt's delayed mana + Improvisation paradigm \"each first main phase\" would need a new BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fired in run_turn). _do_untap_step clears summoning_sick + land_plays_remaining=1.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — _TURN_SEQUENCE; advance_phase empties mana pools each transition; extra_turns FIFO list of seat indices (for Ral −7 skip turns — note: this models EXTRA turns, \"skip turns\" is the inverse and not directly supported).\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py` — create_game(deck1,deck2,scripts=(s1,s2)); set_board_state(game,player_index, battlefield/hand/graveyard/life/mana); cast_spell(game,player_index,card_name,targets) scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft` then engine cast_spell then resolves all stack; declare_attackers(game,names) appendlefts attacker list; declare_blockers(game,{atk:[blk]}). card_colors(card) derives from mana cost.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_205/card_impl.py` + tests.py — Converge reference. `self.colors_spent: int = 0`; tests set int directly; pipeline sets list (handle both).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_244/card_impl.py` + tests.py — Replacement reference (Progenitus). Tests: register adds 1 effect; event_type is MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent; apply with CreatureDiesReplacementEvent redirects to library + prevented.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py` (Kaito) — Planeswalker: register_triggers for passive (DealsDamageTriggeredEvent condition reads event.source/target/combat); get_loyalty_abilities returns [LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1/−2/−9, effect=_fn, description=...)]; uses `getattr(pw,'_resolve_target',None)`; emblem registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_45/card_impl.py` (Kiora) — Attack trigger reference: condition `attacker = event.attacker or event.creature; if attacker is not source: return False`; effect `(game)->None` captures source, uses choose_yes_no + create_token.\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` — authoritative static properties (all 10 confirmed; details in section 2 of analysis). Each stub sets `self.colors = [...]` but FDN references omit colors and pass.\n   - All 10 `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` — currently `class XxxYyy(CardImpl): pass`. Confirmed class names: TheDawningArchaic, TogetherAsOne, EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares, ManaSculpt, RalZarekGuestLecturer, ImprovisationCapstone, LoreholdTheHistorian, SilverquillTheDisputant, WitherbloomTheBalancer, GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None — no code written or executed yet this session. Identified pre-existing converge type inconsistency (int in tests vs list in pipeline) to handle defensively.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed SpellCastTriggeredEvent + AttacksTriggeredEvent are never fired; safe to add firing (test_triggers.py constructs them manually; dormant FDN cards have no tests).\n   - Designed solution for \"effect can't access event\" via stash-in-condition (Silverquill stashes event.spell on self).\n   - Designed \"exile instead of graveyard\" via `_exile_on_graveyard` flag read in `_resolve_spell` (avoids replacement-event complexity since _resolve_spell's stack→graveyard move isn't leaving_battlefield).\n   - Open challenge: \"at beginning of your next main phase\" (Mana Sculpt) and \"each of your first main phases\" (paradigm) have no engine event — would require adding BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent to turn.py; planned best-effort.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (verbatim core): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a