repped sos_stubs.py to lock down authoritative static properties for the final 5 cards (ImprovisationCapstone {5}{R}{R} Lesson; LoreholdTheHistorian {3}{R}{W} Elder Dragon Legendary 5/5; SilverquillTheDisputant {2}{W}{B} Elder Dragon Legendary 4/4; WitherbloomTheBalancer {6}{B}{G} Elder Dragon Legendary 5/5; GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex Land ManaCost()). I finalized the engine-extension plan: (a) fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell (after push) and cast_spell_free with spell=stack_obj; (b) fire AttacksTriggeredEvent per attacker in declare_attackers_step setting both attacker and creature; (c) `_resolve_spell` exile-flag (`_exile_on_graveyard`); (d) loosen move_to_zone replacement gate to `if replacement_event is not None:`; (e) Silverquill casualty via SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger that stashes event.spell in its condition and copies via copy_spell on resolution. No implementation code has been written yet. Next concrete step was to begin implementing the first card (Silverquill) and the engine support it needs.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementing sos_226 Silverquill (task #2, the lowest-complexity starting point) and the engine support it requires. Specifically: (1) Add SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing in `engine/casting.py` `cast_spell()` immediately after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` with `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player)` (and the same in `cast_spell_free`), since I confirmed it is currently never fired. (2) Implement `SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` with name 'Silverquill, the Disputant', mana_cost {2}{W}{B}, subtypes {Elder, Dragon}, supertypes {Legendary}, base_power/toughness 4/4, keywords FLYING|VIGILANCE, and `register_triggers` adding a TriggerRegistration(event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent) whose condition gates on the cast card being an instant/sorcery controlled by Silverquill's controller (stashing the StackObject) and whose effect performs the optional casualty sacrifice (creature power≥1) + copy_spell. This is directly in line with task #2 (\"Implement sos_226 Silverquill (casualty)\") which was in_progress, and the user's explicit instruction that \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics.\" Before editing cast_spell, ensure changes preserve behaviors in `engine_tests/test_casting.py` (firing fire_event with no registered SpellCast triggers is a no-op, so existing tests remain green).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6","uuid":"035d251a-9f68-4722-a2f4-9ea38c130477","timestamp":"2026-05-30T04:15:43.334Z","isSynthetic":true}
