nt sos_4 Together as One (converge)\n   - #5 Implement sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n   - #6 Implement sos_245 Witherbloom (affinity)\n   - #7 Implement sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n   - #8 Implement sos_13 Emeritus of Truce (prepared/MDFC)\n   - #9 Implement sos_120 Improvisation Capstone (paradigm)\n   - #10 Implement sos_201 Lorehold (miracle)\n   - #11 Implement sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker\n   - #12 Write tests and run full suite\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Completing context re-acquisition after compaction. This entire session was reading/verification (no edits): re-read run_manifest.json/prompt.md/PROJECT_MAP.md; loaded task tools; read engine/casting.py, all 10 SOS specs, sos_226 spec+impl, sos_stubs.py (partial), test_utils.py, engine/game.py, mana.py, turn.py, combat.py, zones.py, types.py, player.py, game_state.py, replacement_effects.py, continuous_effects.py, abilities.py, fdn_205/fdn_44/fdn_45/fdn_13 implementations, fdn_13 tests, and engine_tests/test_triggers.py + test_extra_turns.py. The immediate goal confirmed: implement sos_226 Silverquill (task #2, in_progress) plus the engine support to fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in `cast_spell`. No implementation code has been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementing the engine support and the first card, directly continuing task #2 (\"Implement sos_226 Silverquill (casualty)\") which is in_progress, per the user's instruction that \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics.\"\n   Concretely:\n   (a) Edit `engine/casting.py` `cast_spell()` to fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` immediately after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`:\n       `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))` (and the analogous firing in `cast_spell_free`), since I confirmed via test_triggers.py that firing with no registered SpellCast triggers is a no-op and existing engine_tests stay green.\n  