{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory (`cards/sos/sos_<N>/`) contains a `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a `card_impl.py` template (stub class) to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples, refer to `RULEBOOK.txt`, and read engine source modules for API discovery. The user explicitly states: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n   Per-card tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (I create these). Do NOT modify FDN tests. Engine modifications must be additive/behavior-preserving (engine_tests must stay green at 1184 passed).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Casualty (sos_226), Counter+conditional-delayed-mana (sos_57), Converge (sos_4), graveyard-cost-reduction + attack-trigger cast-from-graveyard-with-exile-replacement (sos_1), Affinity for creatures self + granting to instants/sorceries (sos_245), land mana abilities + {5}-becomes-creature (sos_257), Prepared/MDFC token-maker + cast-copy (sos_13), Paradigm/exile-and-cast-from-library (sos_120), Miracle granter + opponent-upkeep loot (sos_201), Planeswalker Surveil/discard/reanimate/coin-flip-skip-turns (sos_97).\n   - Engine: event-driven TriggerManager (condition `(game,event)->bool`; effect `(game)->None` — effect receives ONLY game, must capture via closure or stash on source; isinstance(event,event_type) filters BEFORE condition runs; APNAP ordering); ReplacementManager (\"instead\", inline, only when leaving battlefield); 7-layer EffectManager; LIFO Stack; DeterministicPlayer scripted via `_script` deque (popleft).\n   - Python 3.11.2; run tests with `pytest` (NOT `python`; use `python3` if needed). pytest.ini has \"Unknown config option: timeout\" warning (harmless).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **All 10 SOS oracle texts (verbatim authoritative) and class names (CONFIRMED):**\n     - sos_1 `TheDawningArchaic` {10} Legendary Creature—Avatar 7/7 Reach: \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard.\\nReach\\nWhenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n     - sos_4 `TogetherAsOne` {6} Sorcery: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n     - sos_13 `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares` {1}{W}{W} // {W}, Creature—Cat Cleric // Instant, 3/3, Prepared: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\"\n     - sos_57 `ManaSculpt` {1}{U}{U} Instant: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n     - sos_97 `RalZarekGuestLecturer` {1}{B}{B} Legendary Planeswalker—Ral, loyalty 3: \"+1: Surveil 2.\\n−1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\\n−2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n−7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\"\n     - sos_120 `ImprovisationCapstone` {5}{R}{R} Sorcery—Lesson, Paradigm: \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\\nParadigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n     - sos_201 `LoreholdTheHistorian` {3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 5/5 Flying+Haste: \"Flying, haste\\nEach instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n     - sos_226 `SilverquillTheDisputant` {2}{W}{B} Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 4/4 Flying+Vigilance: \"Flying, vigilance\\nEach instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\"\n     - sos_245 `WitherbloomTheBalancer` {6}{B}{G} Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 5/5 Flying+Deathtouch+Affinity: \"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\\nFlying, deathtouch\\nInstant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n     - sos_257 `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex` Land (empty mana_cost): \"{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\"\n\n   - **`/workspace/engine/casting.py`** (MODIFIED): Added `from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent` to top imports. After payment: added `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc  # type: ignore[attr-defined]`. After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in BOTH cast_spell and cast_spell_free, added firing:\n     ```python\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))\n     ```\n     In _resolve_spell else-branch (instant/sorcery), changed to:\n     ```python\n     dest = (Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n     move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/engine/combat.py`** (MODIFIED): After the attacker-declaration loop in declare_attackers_step, added:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     for attacker in combat.attackers:\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/engine/events.py`** (MODIFIED): BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent now has `player: Any = None`. Added new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with `player: Any = None` and `phase: Any = None`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/engine/turn.py`** (MODIFIED): Upkeep now fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player)`. Added new branch:\n     ```python\n     elif current in ((Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None), (Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)):\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player, phase=game.phase))\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/engine/stack.py`** (MODIFIED): Added after peek():\n     ```python\n     def remove(self, obj: StackObject) -> bool:\n         for i, item in enumerate(self._items):\n             if item is obj:\n                 del self._items[i]\n                 return True\n         return False\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`** (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature). __init__ sets name, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{W}{B}\"), subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, supertypes |= {Supertype.LEGENDARY}, keywords Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE, base_power/toughness 4, `self.colors = [\"B\",\"W\"]`. register_triggers registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger: condition `_is_casualty_spell` checks card has INSTANT/SORCERY, event.controller is source.controller, stashes `source._casualty_spell = event.spell`; effect `_casualty_effect` reads stashed spell, gathers eligible (controller's creatures power≥1), `ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1 — sacrifice a creature?\")`, `ctrl.choose(eligible,...)`, `sacrifice(game, ctrl, chosen)`, `copy_obj = copy_spell(game, spell, ctrl)`, `game.stack.push(copy_obj)`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`** (WRITTEN, has in-progress fix): Defines `_Zap(Instant)` ({R}, deals 3 to chosen_targets[0]). TestSilverquillProperties (name, mana_cost, P/T, keywords, types) + TestSilverquillCasualty (_setup helper, test_casualty_copies_spell expecting p2.life==14, test_casualty_declined expecting 17, test_no_casualty_without_silverquill expecting 17). Imports include ManaType. _setup now has `mana={ManaType.RED: 1}`.\n\n   - **Key engine facts:** Creature has base_power/base_toughness/power/toughness props/plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters/is_attacking/summoning_sick. add_counter supports \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\", else generic dict. create_token sets is_token + fires ETB + registers triggers. ManaCost.cmc = generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid). copy_spell shallow-copies source card, _copy_resolve sets chosen_targets and calls on_resolve (no zone move). move_to_zone fires CreatureDies only if dest==GRAVEYARD. LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description); planeswalkers expose get_loyalty_abilities; targeted loyalty reads `pw._resolve_target`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `python: command not found` → discovered `python3` (3.11.2) and `pytest` at /usr/local/bin/pytest; use `pytest` directly.\n   - `test_utils.TestSetupError: Failed to cast 'Zap': Cannot cast 'Zap' — insufficient mana` (3 behavior tests failed, 5 property tests passed) → _Zap costs {R} but player had no mana. Fix: added `ManaType` import and `mana={ManaType.RED: 1}` to _setup's set_board_state. This fix was applied to _setup but the THIRD test (test_no_casualty_without_silverquill) which has its own inline set_board_state was NOT yet given mana — still needs fixing.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed firing SpellCastTriggeredEvent/AttacksTriggeredEvent/BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent with nothing registered is a no-op; verified 1184 engine_tests stay green after all 5 engine changes.\n   - Designed casualty: condition stashes event.spell on self (safe because fire_event evaluates each condition once per matching event, and isinstance filters by type first); single-stash approach handles one-spell-at-a-time (acceptable for tests).\n   - Designed exile-instead-of-graveyard via `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag in _resolve_spell (since STACK→GRAVEYARD isn't a battlefield-leave, replacement events don't fire there).\n   - Added Stack.remove for \"counter target spell\" (Mana Sculpt).\n   - Added BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent for delayed-mana (Mana Sculpt) and Paradigm recast (Improvisation) — note these only fire under run_turn, not advance_to_phase.\n   - Recorded card.mana_spent in cast_spell for Mana Sculpt; Mana Sculpt should fall back to target's mana_cost.cmc if mana_spent unset.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (verbatim core): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Final message (current turn): the summarization request (\"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY... create a detailed summary...\").\n\n7. Pending Tasks (from TaskList):\n   - #2 [in_progress] Implement sos_226 Silverquill (casualty) — impl done; tests need final fix + pass\n   - #3 Implement sos_57 Mana Sculpt (counter)\n   - #4 Implement sos_4 Together as One (converge)\n   - #5 Implement sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n   - #6 Implement sos_245 Witherbloom (affinity)\n   - #7 Implement sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n   - #8 Implement sos_13 Emeritus of Truce (prepared/MDFC)\n   - #9 Implement sos_120 Improvisation Capstone (paradigm)\n   - #10 Implement sos_201 Lorehold (miracle)\n   - #11 Implement sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker\n   - #12 Write tests and run full suite\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Implementing/verifying Silverquill (sos_226, task #2 in_progress). The card_impl.py is complete. I wrote tests.py and ran it: 5 property tests passed, 3 behavior tests failed with \"insufficient mana\" because `_Zap` costs {R} and players had no mana. I applied two fixes: (a) added `ManaType` to the tests.py import line (`from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Supertype, Zone`), and (b) changed the `_setup` helper's set_board_state call to `set_board_stat