{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6Ryuijvq29Av9gGTdruzn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive report with all findings.\n\n---\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE ENGINE API RESEARCH REPORT\n\nBased on thorough investigation of the MTG engine at /workspace, here are my findings:\n\n### 1. TOKEN CREATION\n\n**Function location:** `/workspace/engine/game.py:353-384`\n\n**How to create a token and put it on the battlefield:**\n\n```python\nfrom engine.game import create_token\nfrom engine.card import Creature\n\n# Create a 1/1 flying token with two colors (White/Black)\ntoken = Creature(\n    name=\"Soldier\",\n    base_power=1,\n    base_toughness=1,\n    keywords=Keyword.FLYING,\n    subtypes={\"Soldier\"}\n)\ntoken.colors = [\"W\", \"B\"]  # White and Black\n\n# Put it on the battlefield\ncreate_token(game, player, token)\n```\n\n**Key implementation details:**\n- **Function signature:** `create_token(game: GameState, player: Player, token: Any) -> None`\n- Sets `token.is_token = True`, `token.owner = player`, `token.controller = player`\n- Adds token directly to battlefield (no zone transition)\n- Fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` BEFORE registering the token's own triggers (prevents self-firing)\n- Then calls `token.register_triggers()` and `token.register_replacement_effects()` if they exist\n- Token is created using the `Creature` class from `/workspace/engine/card.py:275`\n\n**Creature constructor parameters:**\n- `name`, `mana_cost`, `card_types`, `subtypes`, `supertypes`, `keywords`\n- `rules_text`, `owner`, `controller`\n- **`base_power`** and **`base_toughness`** (must provide these for P/T)\n- Creature automatically gets `is_token = False` initially; `create_token()` sets it to `True`\n\n---\n\n### 2. ENTERS-THE-BATTLEFIELD TRIGGERS\n\n**Example card:** `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_98/card_impl.py` (Ambush Wolf)\n\n**EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent fields** (from `/workspace/engine/events.py:28-33`):\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n    permanent: Any = None\n    controller: Any = None\n    card: Any = None\n    creature: Any = None\n```\n\n**How to implement an ETB trigger:**\n\n```python\ndef register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n    from engine.events import EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent\n    \n    source = self\n\n    # Condition: fires only when THIS creature enters\n    def _self_etb_condition(game: Any, event: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n        return event.permanent is source\n\n    # Effect: what happens when the trigger fires\n    def _etb_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        controller = getattr(source, 'controller', None)\n        if controller is None:\n            return\n        # Do effect here...\n\n    controller = getattr(self, 'controller', None) or game.active_player\n    game.trigger_manager.register(\n        TriggerRegistration(\n            event_type=EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent,\n            condition=_self_etb_condition,\n            effect=_etb_effect,\n            source=self,\n            controller=controller,\n        )\n    )\n```\n\n**Key structural points:**\n- The condition closure must check `event.permanent is source` (identity-based, not equality)\n- Condition returns `bool`\n- Effect takes only `game: GameState`, no event parameter\n- For triggered abilities that target, targets are stored on the card via `chosen_targets` attribute during spell casting, before the trigger fires\n\n---\n\n### 3. ETB TARGETING (when trigger needs to choose a target)\n\n**Pattern from:** `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_98/card_impl.py` (Ambush Wolf) and `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_256/card_impl.py` (Meteor Golem)\n\n**For ETB triggers, there are two phases:**\n\n1. **Targeting phase (during spell resolution):** The spell declares targets via `get_targets()` and `chosen_targets` is set before entering the battlefield.\n\n2. **Trigger effect phase:** Inside the effect, retrieve the pre-chosen target:\n\n```python\ndef _get_chosen_target(card: Any, game: Any) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Helper to extract the target chosen during spell casting.\"\"\"\n    chosen = getattr(card, 'chosen_targets', None)\n    if chosen:\n        return chosen[0]\n    return getattr(card, '_resolve_target', None)\n\ndef _etb_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n    target = _get_chosen_target(source, game)\n    if target is not None:\n        # Use the target\n        destroy(game, target)\n```\n\n**For spells with targeting** (cast normally, not just triggers):\n\nInside the spell's `get_targets()` method, return a `TargetRequirement`:\n```python\nfrom engine.types import TargetRequirement, Zone\n\ndef get_targets(self, game: \"GameState\") -> list:\n    return [\n        TargetRequirement(\n            filter_fn=lambda obj: (\n                CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n                and getattr(obj, \"controller\", None) is getattr(self, \"controller\", None)\n            ),\n            description=\"target creature you control\",\n            zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n        )\n    ]\n```\n\n**For inline effect choices** (not spell-level targeting): Use `controller.choose()` or `controller.choose_yes_no()`:\n- **From sos_1 (The Dawning Archaic)** at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py:86-97`:\n```python\nif not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Cast an instant or sorcery from your graveyard for free?\"):\n    return\n\nchosen = ctrl.choose(candidates, \"Choose a card to cast from your graveyard\")\nif chosen is None or chosen not in candidates:\n    return\n```\n\n- **From sos_226 (Silverquill)** at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:80-83`:\n```python\nif not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1 — sacrifice a creature?\"):\n    return\n\nchosen = ctrl.choose(eligible, \"Choose a creature to sacrifice (casualty)\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. CASTING FROM EXILE\n\n**Function location:** `/workspace/engine/casting.py:280-406`\n\n**Signature:**\n```python\ndef cast_spell_free(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Player,\n    card: CardImpl,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n) -> None:\n```\n\n**Yes, it accepts arbitrary zones like Zone.EXILE.** The function works for any zone.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Moves card from `from_zone` to player's stack zone\n2. Optionally chooses targets\n3. Calls `card.on_cast(game)`\n4. Pushes a `StackObject` onto the stack\n5. Fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n6. **The spell goes through the stack and can be countered**\n7. On resolution: permanents → battlefield, non-permanents → graveyard\n\n**Usage example from sos_1** (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py:97`):\n```python\nchosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True  # Custom flag to redirect graveyard to exile\ncast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n```\n\n**To move card TO exile**, use `/workspace/engine/zones.py:179-326`:\n\n```python\ndef move_to_zone(\n    game: GameState,\n    card: Any,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n    to_zone: Zone,\n    *,\n    replacement_event: Any | None = None,\n) -> None:\n```\n\nOr the helper in `engine/game.py:267-291`:\n```python\ndef exile(game: GameState, obj: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Exile *obj* — move it to its owner's exile zone.\"\"\"\n    # Automatically finds which zone obj is in and moves to EXILE\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING SOS CARD STRUCTURES\n\n#### **sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)** - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` (Full file 1-100)\n\n**Key structural elements:**\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\nclass SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature):\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        # Standard pattern: use setdefault for all properties\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Silverquill, the Disputant\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{W}{B}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"})\n        # Supertypes need special merging\n        kwargs[\"supertypes\"] = (kwargs.get(\"supertypes\") or set()) | {Supertype.LEGENDARY}\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"rules_text\", \"...\")\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n        self.colors = [\"B\", \"W\"]  # Colors as list\n\n    def register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        \"\"\"Grant casualty 1 to instant/sorcery spells the controller casts.\"\"\"\n        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n        source = self\n        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n\n        # Condition closure\n        def _is_casualty_spell(game: Any, event: SpellCastTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n            card = event.card\n            if card is None:\n                return False\n            types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n            if CardType.INSTANT not in types and CardType.SORCERY not in types:\n                return False\n            if event.controller is not source.controller:\n                return False\n            # Stash spell for effect callback\n            source._casualty_spell = event.spell\n            return True\n\n        # Effect closure\n        def _casualty_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            from engine.game import sacrifice\n            from engine.stack import copy_spell\n            from engine.types import Zone\n\n            spell = getattr(source, \"_casualty_spell\", None)\n            source._casualty_spell = None\n            ctrl = source.controller\n            if spell is None or ctrl is None:\n                return\n\n            eligible = [c for c in ctrl.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all() ...]\n            if not eligible:\n                return\n\n            if not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1 — sacrifice a creature?\"):\n                return\n\n            chosen = ctrl.choose(eligible, \"Choose a creature to sacrifice (casualty)\")\n            if chosen is None or chosen not in eligible:\n                return\n\n            sacrifice(game, ctrl, chosen)\n            copy_obj = copy_spell(game, spell, ctrl)\n            game.stack.push(copy_obj)\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_is_casualty_spell,\n                effect=_casualty_effect,\n                source=self,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n```\n\n**Pattern observations:**\n- All trigger closures capture `source = self` for identity-safe references\n- All effects import needed functions inside the closure (lazy imports)\n- Conditions can modify the `source` object to pass data to effects (e.g., `source._casualty_spell = event.spell`)\n- Use `getattr(card, \"attribute\", default)` to safely access optional properties\n- Player choices via `controller.choose_yes_no()` and `controller.choose(list, prompt)`\n\n#### **sos_1 (The Dawning Archaic)** - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` (Full file 1-108)\n\n**Key structural elements:**\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype, Zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\n# Helper function (module-level, reusable)\ndef _is_instant_or_sorcery(card: Any) -> bool:\n    types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n    return CardType.INSTANT in types or CardType.SORCERY in types\n\nclass TheDawningArchaic(Creature):\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"The Dawning Archaic\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Avatar\"})\n        kwargs[\"supertypes\"] = (kwargs.get(\"supertypes\") or set()) | {Supertype.LEGENDARY}\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.REACH)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 7)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 7)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"rules_text\", \"...\")\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n        self.colors = []\n\n    def cost_reduction(self, game: \"GameState\") -> int:\n        \"\"\"Cost reduction hook — engine calls this during casting.\"\"\"\n        controller = self.controller\n        if controller is None:\n            return 0\n        return sum(\n            1\n            for card in controller.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].get_all()\n            if _is_instant_or_sorcery(card)\n        )\n\n    def register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        \"\"\"Attack trigger: free-cast an instant/sorcery from the graveyard.\"\"\"\n        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n        source = self\n        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n\n        def _attack_condition(game: Any, event: AttacksTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n            return event.creature is source\n\n        def _attack_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None:\n                return\n\n            candidates = [\n                c\n                for c in ctrl.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].get_all()\n                if _is_instant_or_sorcery(c)\n            ]\n            if not candidates:\n                return\n\n            if not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Cast an instant or sorcery from your graveyard for free?\"):\n                return\n\n            chosen = ctrl.choose(candidates, \"Choose a card to cast from your graveyard\")\n            if chosen is None or chosen not in candidates:\n                return\n\n            # Custom flag for replacement effect handling\n            chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True\n            cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=AttacksTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_attack_condition,\n                effect=_attack_effect,\n                source=self,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n```\n\n**Pattern observations:**\n- Module-level helper functions (e.g., `_is_instant_or_sorcery`) for shared logic\n- **`cost_reduction(game)`** hook — engine queries this before paying mana to cast the card\n- **`register_triggers(game)`** — called when card enters battlefield or when card exists on battlefield for permanent triggers\n- Custom attributes can be set on cards as flags (e.g., `chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True`)\n- Use `controller.choose()` to let player pick from a list of candidates\n- Import functions inside effect closures to keep code modular\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY\n\nAll key APIs identified:\n\n1. **Token creation:** `create_token(game, player, token_object)` — creates a `Creature` instance with `base_power`/`base_toughness` and two colors via `token.colors = [\"W\", \"B\"]`\n\n2. **ETB triggers:** Register via `TriggerRegistration` with `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, condition checks `event.permanent is source`, effect receives only `game`\n\n3. **ETB targeting:** Targets chosen during spell cast are stored in `card.chosen_targets` list; retrieve in effect via `getattr(card, 'chosen_targets', None)`\n\n4. **Free casting:** `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, Zone.EXILE)` accepts any source zone and puts spell on stack (counterable)\n\n5. **SOS card structure:** Inherit from `Creature`, use `setdefault()` for initialization, implement `register_triggers()` with closure pattern, use `controller.choose()` for UI choices"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6","uuid":"52258f42-13cc-43d1-a569-529b0b4c1db3","timestamp":"2026-05-30T04:55:41.955Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm implementing a Magic: The Gathering card in a Python engine at /workspace. I need to understand several engine APIs by finding concrete usage examples. Please investigate and report findings concisely (with file paths and line numbers, and short code snippets).\n\n1. TOKEN CREATION: How are creature tokens created and put onto the battlefield in this engine? Look for any helper like `create_token`, `make_token`, or cards that create tokens (e.g. search cards/fdn/ for token creation). I need to know: what function/class to use, and how a 1/1 flying creature token with two colors would be constructed and added to a player's battlefield. Search engine/ (game.py, game_state.py, tokens.py if it exists) and cards/fdn/*/card_impl.py.\n\n2. ENTERS-THE-BATTLEFIELD TRIGGERS: Find a card in cards/fdn/ that has a \"When this creature enters, ...\" triggered ability. Show how it implements register_triggers using EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent — specifically the condition (how it checks the entering permanent is itself) and the effect. Note the exact fields of EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent (it has permanent, controller, card, creature per engine/events.py).\n\n3. ETB TARGETING: When an ETB trigger needs to choose a target (e.g. \"target player\"), how is that done inside the trigger effect? Triggered abilities don't get engine-level targeting — show how existing cards pick targets inside the effect via controller.choose / choose_target. Look at cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py (The Dawning Archaic) which I already wrote and uses choose_yes_no/choose inside an attack trigger, and any fdn card that targets in an ETB.\n\n4. CASTING FROM EXILE: Find `cast_spell_free` and any mechanism to cast a card from the EXILE zone. I previously used cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD) in sos_1. Show the signature of cast_spell_free in engine/casting.py and whether it accepts an arbitrary source zone like Zone.EXILE. Also show how engine/zones.py move_to_zone works for putting a card into exile.\n\n5. HOW EXISTING SOS CARDS ARE STRUCTURED: Read cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py fully (Silverquill — casualty) and cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py fully (The Dawning Archaic) so I can see the exact import style, helper-function patterns, and how triggers/effects are written in this project. Quote the key structural parts.\n\nReport all findings in one organized response. Do NOT write or modify any files — this is research only.","agentId":"ae2e5262d7653e5b5","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive report with all findings.\n\n---\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE ENGINE API RESEARCH REPORT\n\nBased on thorough investigation of the MTG engine at /workspace, here are my findings:\n\n### 1. TOKEN CREATION\n\n**Function location:** `/workspace/engine/game.py:353-384`\n\n**How to create a token and put it on the battlefield:**\n\n```python\nfrom engine.game import create_token\nfrom engine.card import Creature\n\n# Create a 1/1 flying token with two colors (White/Black)\ntoken = Creature(\n    name=\"Soldier\",\n    base_power=1,\n    base_toughness=1,\n    keywords=Keyword.FLYING,\n    subtypes={\"Soldier\"}\n)\ntoken.colors = [\"W\", \"B\"]  # White and Black\n\n# Put it on the battlefield\ncreate_token(game, player, token)\n```\n\n**Key implementation details:**\n- **Function signature:** `create_token(game: GameState, player: Player, token: Any) -> None`\n- Sets `token.is_token = True`, `token.owner = player`, `token.controller = player`\n- Adds token directly to battlefield (no zone transition)\n- Fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` BEFORE registering the token's own triggers (prevents self-firing)\n- Then calls `token.register_triggers()` and `token.register_replacement_effects()` if they exist\n- Token is created using the `Creature` class from `/workspace/engine/card.py:275`\n\n**Creature constructor parameters:**\n- `name`, `mana_cost`, `card_types`, `subtypes`, `supertypes`, `keywords`\n- `rules_text`, `owner`, `controller`\n- **`base_power`** and **`base_toughness`** (must provide these for P/T)\n- Creature automatically gets `is_token = False` initially; `create_token()` sets it to `True`\n\n---\n\n### 2. ENTERS-THE-BATTLEFIELD TRIGGERS\n\n**Example card:** `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_98/card_impl.py` (Ambush Wolf)\n\n**EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent fields** (from `/workspace/engine/events.py:28-33`):\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n    permanent: Any = None\n    controller: Any = None\n    card: Any = None\n    creature: Any = None\n```\n\n**How to implement an ETB trigger:**\n\n```python\ndef register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n    from engine.events import EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent\n    \n    source = self\n\n    # Condition: fires only when THIS creature enters\n    def _self_etb_condition(game: Any, event: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n        return event.permanent is source\n\n    # Effect: what happens when the trigger fires\n    def _etb_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        controller = getattr(source, 'controller', None)\n        if controller is None:\n            return\n        # Do effect here...\n\n    controller = getattr(self, 'controller', None) or game.active_player\n    game.trigger_manager.register(\n        TriggerRegistration(\n            event_type=EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent,\n            condition=_self_etb_condition,\n            effect=_etb_effect,\n            source=self,\n            controller=controller,\n        )\n    )\n```\n\n**Key structural points:**\n- The condition closure must check `event.permanent is source` (identity-based, not equality)\n- Condition returns `bool`\n- Effect takes only `game: GameState`, no event parameter\n- For triggered abilities that target, targets are stored on the card via `chosen_targets` attribute during spell casting, before the trigger fires\n\n---\n\n### 3. ETB TARGETING (when trigger needs to choose a target)\n\n**Pattern from:** `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_98/card_impl.py` (Ambush Wolf) and `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_256/card_impl.py` (Meteor Golem)\n\n**For ETB triggers, there are two phases:**\n\n1. **Targeting phase (during spell resolution):** The spell declares targets via `get_targets()` and `chosen_targets` is set before entering the battlefield.\n\n2. **Trigger effect phase:** Inside the effect, retrieve the pre-chosen target:\n\n```python\ndef _get_chosen_target(card: Any, game: Any) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Helper to extract the target chosen during spell casting.\"\"\"\n    chosen = getattr(card, 'chosen_targets', None)\n    if chosen:\n        return chosen[0]\n    return getattr(card, '_resolve_target', None)\n\ndef _etb_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n    target = _get_chosen_target(source, game)\n    if target is not None:\n        # Use the target\n        destroy(game, target)\n```\n\n**For spells with targeting** (cast normally, not just triggers):\n\nInside the spell's `get_targets()` method, return a `TargetRequirement`:\n```python\nfrom engine.types import TargetRequirement, Zone\n\ndef get_targets(self, game: \"GameState\") -> list:\n    return [\n        TargetRequirement(\n            filter_fn=lambda obj: (\n                CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n                and getattr(obj, \"controller\", None) is getattr(self, \"controller\", None)\n            ),\n            description=\"target creature you control\",\n            zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n        )\n    ]\n```\n\n**For inline effect choices** (not spell-level targeting): Use `controller.choose()` or `controller.choose_yes_no()`:\n- **From sos_1 (The Dawning Archaic)** at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py:86-97`:\n```python\nif not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Cast an instant or sorcery from your graveyard for free?\"):\n    return\n\nchosen = ctrl.choose(candidates, \"Choose a card to cast from your graveyard\")\nif chosen is None or chosen not in candidates:\n    return\n```\n\n- **From sos_226 (Silverquill)** at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:80-83`:\n```python\nif not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1 — sacrifice a creature?\"):\n    return\n\nchosen = ctrl.choose(eligible, \"Choose a creature to sacrifice (casualty)\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. CASTING FROM EXILE\n\n**Function location:** `/workspace/engine/casting.py:280-406`\n\n**Signature:**\n```python\ndef cast_spell_free(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Player,\n    card: CardImpl,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n) -> None:\n```\n\n**Yes, it accepts arbitrary zones like Zone.EXILE.** The function works for any zone.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Moves card from `from_zone` to player's stack zone\n2. Optionally chooses targets\n3. Calls `card.on_cast(game)`\n4. Pushes a `StackObject` onto the stack\n5. Fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n6. **The spell goes through the stack and can be countered**\n7. On resolution: permanents → battlefield, non-permanents → graveyard\n\n**Usage example from sos_1** (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py:97`):\n```python\nchosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True  # Custom flag to redirect graveyard to exile\ncast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n```\n\n**To move card TO exile**, use `/workspace/engine/zones.py:179-326`:\n\n```python\ndef move_to_zone(\n    game: GameState,\n    card: Any,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n    to_zone: Zone,\n    *,\n    replacement_event: Any | None = None,\n) -> None:\n```\n\nOr the helper in `engine/game.py:267-291`:\n```python\ndef exile(game: GameState, obj: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Exile *obj* — move it to its owner's exile zone.\"\"\"\n    # Automatically finds which zone obj is in and moves to EXILE\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING SOS CARD STRUCTURES\n\n#### **sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)** - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` (Full file 1-100)\n\n**Key structural elements:**\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\nclass SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature):\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        # Standard pattern: use setdefault for all properties\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Silverquill, the Disputant\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{W}{B}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"})\n        # Supertypes need special merging\n        kwargs[\"supertypes\"] = (kwargs.get(\"supertypes\") or set()) | {Supertype.LEGENDARY}\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"rules_text\", \"...\")\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n        self.colors = [\"B\", \"W\"]  # Colors as list\n\n    def register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        \"\"\"Grant casualty 1 to instant/sorcery spells the controller casts.\"\"\"\n        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n        source = self\n        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n\n        # Condition closure\n        def _is_casualty_spell(game: Any, event: SpellCastTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n            card = event.card\n            if card is None:\n                return False\n            types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n            if CardType.INSTANT not in types and CardType.SORCERY not in types:\n                return False\n            if event.controller is not source.controller:\n                return False\n            # Stash spell for effect callback\n            source._casualty_spell = event.spell\n            return True\n\n        # Effect closure\n        def _casualty_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            from engine.game import sacrifice\n            from engine.stack import copy_spell\n            from engine.types import Zone\n\n            spell = getattr(source, \"_casualty_spell\", None)\n            source._casualty_spell = None\n            ctrl = source.controller\n            if spell is None or ctrl is None:\n                return\n\n            eligible = [c for c in ctrl.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all() ...]\n            if not eligible:\n                return\n\n            if not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Casualty 1 — sacrifice a creature?\"):\n                return\n\n            chosen = ctrl.choose(eligible, \"Choose a creature to sacrifice (casualty)\")\n            if chosen is None or chosen not in eligible:\n                return\n\n            sacrifice(game, ctrl, chosen)\n            copy_obj = copy_spell(game, spell, ctrl)\n            game.stack.push(copy_obj)\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_is_casualty_spell,\n                effect=_casualty_effect,\n                source=self,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n```\n\n**Pattern observations:**\n- All trigger closures capture `source = self` for identity-safe references\n- All effects import needed functions inside the closure (lazy imports)\n- Conditions can modify the `source` object to pass data to effects (e.g., `source._casualty_spell = event.spell`)\n- Use `getattr(card, \"attribute\", default)` to safely access optional properties\n- Player choices via `controller.choose_yes_no()` and `controller.choose(list, prompt)`\n\n#### **sos_1 (The Dawning Archaic)** - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` (Full file 1-108)\n\n**Key structural elements:**\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype, Zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\n# Helper function (module-level, reusable)\ndef _is_instant_or_sorcery(card: Any) -> bool:\n    types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n    return CardType.INSTANT in types or CardType.SORCERY in types\n\nclass TheDawningArchaic(Creature):\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"The Dawning Archaic\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Avatar\"})\n        kwargs[\"supertypes\"] = (kwargs.get(\"supertypes\") or set()) | {Supertype.LEGENDARY}\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.REACH)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 7)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 7)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"rules_text\", \"...\")\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n        self.colors = []\n\n    def cost_reduction(self, game: \"GameState\") -> int:\n        \"\"\"Cost reduction hook — engine calls this during casting.\"\"\"\n        controller = self.controller\n        if controller is None:\n            return 0\n        return sum(\n            1\n            for card in controller.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].get_all()\n            if _is_instant_or_sorcery(card)\n        )\n\n    def register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        \"\"\"Attack trigger: free-cast an instant/sorcery from the graveyard.\"\"\"\n        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n        source = self\n        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n\n        def _attack_condition(game: Any, event: AttacksTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n            return event.creature is source\n\n        def _attack_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None:\n                return\n\n            candidates = [\n                c\n                for c in ctrl.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].get_all()\n                if _is_instant_or_sorcery(c)\n            ]\n            if not candidates:\n                return\n\n            if not ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Cast an instant or sorcery from your graveyard for free?\"):\n                return\n\n            chosen = ctrl.choose(candidates, \"Choose a card to cast from your graveyard\")\n            if chosen is None or chosen not in candidates:\n                return\n\n            # Custom flag for replacement effect handling\n            chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True\n            cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=AttacksTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_attack_condition,\n                effect=_attack_effect,\n                source=self,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n```\n\n**Pattern observations:**\n- Module-level helper functions (e.g., `_is_instant_or_sorcery`) for shared logic\n- **`cost_reduction(game)`** hook — engine queries this before paying mana to cast the card\n- **`register_triggers(game)`** — called when card enters battlefield or when card exists on battlefield for permanent triggers\n- Custom attributes can be set on cards as flags (e.g., `chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True`)\n- Use `controller.choose()` to let player pick from a list of candidates\n- Import functions inside effect closures to keep code modular\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY\n\nAll key APIs identified:\n\n1. **Token creation:** `create_token(game, player, token_object)` — creates a `Creature` instance with `base_power`/`base_toughness` and two colors via `token.colors = [\"W\", \"B\"]`\n\n2. **ETB triggers:** Register via `TriggerRegistration` with `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, condition checks `event.permanent is source`, effect receives only `game`\n\n3. **ETB targeting:** Targets chosen during spell cast are stored in `card.chosen_targets` list; retrieve in effect via `getattr(card, 'chosen_targets', None)`\n\n4. **Free casting:** `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, Zone.EXILE)` accepts any source zone and puts spell on stack (counterable)\n\n5. **SOS card structure:** Inherit from `Creature`, use `setdefault()` for initialization, implement `register_triggers()` with closure pattern, use `controller.choose()` for UI choices"}],"totalDurationMs":79192,"totalTokens":64987,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5216,"cache_read_input_tokens":55349,"output_tokens":4419,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5216},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":4419,"cache_read_input_tokens":55349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5216,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":16,"searchCount":6,"bashCount":11,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
