{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory (`cards/sos/sos_<N>/`) contains a `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a `card_impl.py` template stub class to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples, refer to `RULEBOOK.txt`, and read engine source modules directly for API discovery. The user stated: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n   Per-card tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (I create these). Do NOT modify FDN tests. Engine modifications must be additive/behavior-preserving. The engine_tests baseline is 1145 passed (must stay 1145). Cards 226, 57, 4, 1, 245, 257 were completed in prior sessions. This session: completed 13 and 120; in progress on 201; remaining: 97 (Ral Zarek planeswalker) and #12 (run full suite).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Preparation/Prepared designation (sos_13 ✓ this session), Paradigm (sos_120 ✓ this session), Miracle granter + loot (sos_201 in progress), Planeswalker (sos_97 pending). Plus prior: Casualty, Counter+delayed-mana, Converge, graveyard-recast, Affinity, land-animation.\n   - Card class hierarchy (engine/card.py): `Creature` has base_power/base_toughness, modified_power/modified_toughness, properties `power`/`toughness` = modified + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters. `Instant`/`Sorcery` add their CardType. `_reset_characteristics()` resets card_types to `_original_card_types` and keywords (subtypes NOT reset). NOTE: TWO `ContinuousEffect` classes exist (engine.card with apply/remove/description vs engine.continuous_effects with source/layer/sublayer/apply/duration).\n   - Casting (engine/casting.py): `cast_spell(game, player, card)` is HAND-ONLY, charges mana, applies get_cost_reduction. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` works from ANY zone (incl HAND, EXILE), NO mana charge, calls `card.get_targets(game)` then `player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)` per spec, validates via `filter_fn(target)` (single-arg), pushes StackObject, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets` BEFORE on_resolve, then permanents→battlefield, instant/sorcery→graveyard (or EXILE if `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard` is True).\n   - Triggers (engine/triggers.py): `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`. `fire_event` filters by isinstance + condition, then pushes a `StackObject(source, controller, on_resolve=trigger.effect)` in APNAP order. Effect signature is `(game) -> None` — NO event passed. To pass event data to the effect, use the mutable-cell pattern (set a list cell in the condition, read in the effect) — established in fdn_58: `_last_amount = [0]` set in `_cond`, read in `_eff`. `get_triggers()`, `get_triggers_for_source(source)`, `unregister(source)` (identity-based).\n   - Events (engine/events.py): EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, card, creature), GainsLifeTriggeredEvent(player, amount), DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card), BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player), BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, phase), SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller).\n   - State-based actions: `_sba_token_not_on_battlefield` (state_based_actions.py:189) removes any object with `is_token=True` from ALL non-battlefield zones INCLUDING EXILE, HAND, GRAVEYARD, LIBRARY, STACK, COMMAND. CRITICAL: a copy that must persist in exile (e.g., a prepared copy) must NOT be is_token; a copy that should cease to exist after resolution can be marked is_token so the next SBA sweep removes it from the graveyard.\n   - ZoneContainer (engine/zones.py): index 0 = bottom, index -1 = top. `add(obj, position=\"top\")` appends; `top(n)` returns last n; `remove`/`contains`/`get_all`/`__len__`. `move_to_zone` fires ETB before register_triggers.\n   - game.py helpers: `exile(game, obj)`, `draw_card(game, player)` (increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent), `discard(game, player, card)`, `create_token(game, player, token)` (sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to battlefield, fires ETB BEFORE register_triggers). NO `gain_life` helper — use `controller.life += amount` + fire GainsLifeTriggeredEvent.\n   - `cards_drawn_this_turn` was incremented in draw_card but NEVER reset; `create_game` draws 7 via draw_card so it starts at 7. game.turn_number exists.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: scripted via `_script` deque; choose/choose_yes_no/choose_target/choose_card all `_pop()` (popleft). Construct game with `create_game(scripts=([...], [...]))`; append more answers via `player._script.append(x)`.\n   - test_utils: `create_game`, `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)` (NO library param — set library directly via `player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY].add(card)`), `cast_spell`, `_resolve_top_of_stack`.\n   - Keyword Flag enum (types.py:97) has only evergreen keywords (FLYING, HASTE, DEATHTOUCH, FLASH, PROWESS, etc.) — NO PREPARED/MIRACLE/PARADIGM. registry.py treats `keywords` as plain metadata strings (no conformance test forces enum membership). ManaType: WHITE/BLUE/BLACK/RED/GREEN/COLORLESS. Supertype.LEGENDARY.\n   - Python 3.11; run tests with bare `pytest` (NOT `python`/`python -m pytest`). \"Unknown config option: timeout\" warning is harmless. `Keyword.FLYING in card.keywords` works (3.11 Flag membership).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` (CREATED THIS SESSION, COMPLETE, 17 tests pass):\n     - Models \"prepared\" as `self.prepared` boolean (no engine change). The prepared copy lives in exile as a NON-token Instant (so SBA doesn't remove it from exile); the copy sets `self.is_token = True` in its own `on_resolve` so it ceases to exist after resolving to the graveyard.\n     - Helpers: `_creatures_controlled(player)`, `_on_battlefield(game, obj)`.\n     - `_SwordsToPlowshares(Instant)`: name \"Swords to Plowshares\", {W}, colors [\"W\"]. `get_targets` returns `[TargetRequirement(filter_fn=_is_target_creature, description=\"target creature\", zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD)]` where `_is_target_creature` checks CardType.CREATURE + `_on_battlefield`. `on_resolve`: reads `self.chosen_targets[0]`, computes power before exile, calls `exile(game, target)`, then `controller.life += power` + fires `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent(player=controller, amount=power)`, then `self.is_token = True`.\n     - `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`: name=\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\", {1}{W}{W}, subtypes {Cat, Cleric}, base_power=3, base_toughness=3, colors=[\"W\"], self.prepared=False, self._stp_copy=None. `register_triggers`: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent, condition `event.permanent is source`; effect uses `controller.choose(list(game.players), ...)` to pick target player, creates Inkling token (Creature 1/1, subtypes {\"Inkling\"}, keywords Keyword.FLYING, colors=[\"W\",\"B\"]) via `create_token`, then if `any(_creatures_controlled(p) > _creatures_controlled(controller) for p in game.players if p is not controller)` calls `source._become_prepared(game)`. `_become_prepared(game)`: guarded by `if self.prepared: return`, creates `_SwordsToPlowshares(owner=controller, controller=controller)` added to `controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]`, sets prepared=True, stores _stp_copy. `can_cast_prepared(game)`: returns True only if prepared, copy in controller's exile, and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(copy.mana_cost)`. `cast_prepared(game)`: if not can_cast_prepared return False; pays {W}, sets prepared=False and _stp_copy=None, then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, copy, Zone.EXILE)`, returns True.\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (CREATED THIS SESSION, 17 tests pass): Helpers `_emeritus`, `_bear(player, name, power)`, `_resolve_stack(game)` (pop + on_resolve + resolve_state_based_actions), `_inklings`, `_stp_in_exile`. Classes: TestEmeritusProperties (name, mana_cost, power_toughness, types_and_colors, starts_unprepared), TestEmeritusETB (with `_fire_etb` helper: `emeritus.register_triggers(game); fire_event(EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent=emeritus, controller=controller)); _resolve_stack`; tests: creates_inkling_for_chosen_player, inkling_token_characteristics, token_can_go_to_opponent, becomes_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures [p1 has emeritus, p2 has 3 bears, token to self], not_prepared_when_you_have_at_least_as_many, become_prepared_is_idempotent), TestSwordsToPlowsharesProperties, TestCastPrepared (with `_prepared_setup` giving mana {W:1} + `_become_prepared`; tests: cannot_cast_when_not_prepared, cannot_cast_without_mana, cast_prepared_exiles_creature_and_gains_life [bear power 4, p2.life 20→24], cast_prepared_unprepares, cast_copy_ceases_to_exist_after_resolution). IMPORTANT: import line is `from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone` (ManaType was missing initially → fixed).\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` (CREATED THIS SESSION, COMPLETE, 15 tests pass):\n     - Helpers: `_cmc(card)`, `_is_castable_spell(card)` (CardType.LAND not in card_types).\n     - `ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery)`: name=\"Improvisation Capstone\", {5}{R}{R}, subtypes {\"Lesson\"}, colors=[\"R\"]. `on_resolve`: `_resolve_main_effect`, then `self._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True`, then `_setup_paradigm`. `_exile_until_mv(controller, threshold)` (staticmethod): exiles `library.top(1)[0]` until `total >= 4`. `_offer_free_casts(game, controller, candidates)` (staticmethod): for each non-land still in exile, `if controller.choose_yes_no(...): cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. `_setup_paradigm(game, controller)`: guarded by `controller._paradigm_active_names` set keyed by self.name; registers persistent BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger with sentinel source, condition `event.player is controller and event.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`, effect creates `cls(owner=controller, controller=controller)` copy with `copy.is_token = True` added to exile, then optional `choose_yes_no` → cast_spell_free.\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` (CREATED THIS SESSION, 15 tests pass): Helpers `_capstone`, `_spell(player, name, cmc)` (Instant with ManaCost(generic=cmc)), `_creature(player, name, cmc)`, `_set_library(game, player, cards)` (direct library manipulation, last item = top), `_resolve_stack`, `_main_phase_triggers`, `_capstone_copies_in_exile`. Classes: TestCapstoneProperties, TestMainEffect (exiles_until_total_mv_at_least_four, stops_as_soon_as_threshold_met, handles_empty_library, may_cast_exiled_spell_for_free, uncast_exiled_spells_remain_in_exile), TestParadigm (spell_redirected_to_exile asserts `cap._exile_instead_of_graveyard is True`, first_resolution_registers_recast_trigger, paradigm_setup_only_once, recast_copy_at_precombat_main [scripts [True, True], stocks library after first resolve], no_recast_when_declined, no_recast_on_postcombat_main, no_recast_on_opponents_main).\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` (MODIFIED THIS SESSION — additive engine change): Added per-turn reset of `cards_drawn_this_turn` in `_do_untap_step` after the land_plays_remaining reset:\n     ```python\n     # Reset land plays for the active player\n     active.land_plays_remaining = 1\n\n     # A new turn has begun: reset every player's per-turn draw count so that\n     # \"first card you've drawn this turn\" mechanics (e.g. miracle) work.\n     for player in game.players:\n         player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0\n     ```\n     Justification: counter was incremented in draw_card but never reset; no engine_test reads it (verified via grep); needed for miracle \"first card this turn\".\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (CREATED THIS SESSION — MOST RECENT, tests NOT yet written/run):\n     - Module constant `_MIRACLE_COST = ManaCost(generic=2)`. Helpers `_on_battlefield(game, obj)`, `_is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`.\n     - `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`: name=\"Lorehold, the Historian\", {3}{R}{W}, subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, supertypes |= {Supertype.LEGENDARY}, keywords Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE, base_power=5, base_toughness=5, colors=[\"R\",\"W\"].\n     - `register_triggers(game)`: calls `_register_miracle(game, source, controller)` and `_register_loot(game, source, controller)`.\n     - `_register_miracle`: uses mutable cell `drawn = [None]`. Condition (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent): on_battlefield + `event.player is source.controller` + card is instant/sorcery + `owner.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`; sets `drawn[0] = card`; returns True. Effect: if card still in hand and `owner.mana_pool.can_pay(_MIRACLE_COST)` and `owner.choose_yes_no(...)`: pay {2} then `cast_spell_free(game, owner, card, Zone.HAND)`.\n     - `_register_loot`: Condition (BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent): on_battlefield + `upkeep_player is not None and upkeep_player is not owner`. Effect: if hand non-empty and `owner.choose_yes_no(\"Discard a card to draw a card?\")`: `card = owner.choose_card(hand.get_all(), ...)`; if in hand: `discard(game, owner, card)` then `draw_card(game, owner)`.\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_spec.json` (READ): name \"Lorehold, the Historian\", {3}{R}{W}, Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors [R,W], keywords [Flying, Haste], oracle text: \"Flying, haste\\nEach instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\", expert.\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_spec.json` (NOT YET READ): Ral Zarek Guest Lecturer, planeswalker (per prior summary: {1}{B}{B} — needs verification).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - sos_13 tests.py first run: `NameError: name 'ManaType' is not defined` (4 failures in TestCastPrepared using `mana={ManaType.WHITE: 1}`). FIXED by changing import to `from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone`. Re-ran: 17 passed.\n   - No other errors this session (sos_120 passed 15/15 first try).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - sos_13 prepared-copy lifecycle: solved the conflict that `_sba_token_not_on_battlefield` removes tokens from EXILE (so prepared copy can't be a token in exile) vs. wanting the cast copy to cease to exist (set `is_token=True` only inside the copy's `on_resolve`, so it's removed only after resolving to the graveyard, never while waiting in exile).\n   - sos_120 Paradigm recast: persistent BeginningOfMainPhase trigger guarded by `controller._paradigm_active_names` (registers once = \"first time\"); per-turn copies are is_token so declined/resolved copies are swept by SBA. Verified no infinite loop (recast fires only on main-phase event, not on cast).\n   - sos_201 miracle \"first card this turn\": discovered `cards_drawn_this_turn` is never reset (create_game leaves it at 7). Fixed by adding an additive reset to `_do_untap_step` for all players; verified no engine_test reads the counter. Miracle modeled via cast_spell_free from HAND after manually paying {2} (since cast_spell charges full cost and cast_spell_free charges nothing).\n   - Decided NOT to add Keyword.PREPARED/MIRACLE/PARADIGM enums — designations/granted-keywords modeled via instance attributes; registry keywords are plain strings, no conformance test.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The session began with system-reminders containing Read tool results (sos_257 and sos_245 files) plus the continuation/summary of the prior conversation. There were no new substantive user instructions beyond the carried-over task (implement the 10 cards) and constraints.\n   - Recurring system-reminders listing task tools and current task state (#1–#12).\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch for TaskUpdate, TaskList).\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\" (the summarization request).\n   - Security/process constraints (carried, still in effect verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" And: engine changes must be additive/behavior-preserving; engine_tests must stay at 1145.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - #10 [in_progress] Implement sos_201 Lorehold (miracle) — card_impl.py written; NEED tests.py + run.\n   - #11 [pending] Implement sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker.\n   - #12 [pending] Write tests and run full suite: `pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q`; confirm engine_tests stay at 1145 (especially after the turn.py change).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just finished writing `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (LoreholdTheHistorian) implementing miracle {2} granting (via DrawsCardTriggeredEvent trigger with mutable-cell pattern, conditional on `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`, casting via pay-{2}-then-cast_spell_free-from-HAND) and the opponent-upkeep loot ability (BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent, discard-then-draw). Immediately before this, I made the additive engine change to `/workspace/engine/turn.py` `_do_untap_step` to reset `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for all players at the start of each turn, which is required for miracle's \"first card you've drawn this turn\" semantics. Tasks #9 was marked completed and #10 marked in_progress. The sos_201 tests have NOT yet been written or run, and engine_tests have NOT yet been re-run to confirm the turn.py change preserves the 1145 baseline.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` and run it, then run `pytest engine_tests/ -q` to confirm the turn.py `cards_drawn_this_turn` reset preserves 1145. This directly continues task #10 (in_progress, \"Implement sos_201 Lorehold (miracle)\"). Tests should cover: properties (name, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, FLYING+HASTE, LEGENDARY, {Elder,Dragon}, colors [R,W]); miracle — first drawn instant/sorcery with Lorehold on battlefield + mana {2} → choose_yes_no True casts it for {2} (set `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` then call `draw_card` so it becomes 1; library top is the instant); miracle does NOT apply to a non-first draw, to non-instant/sorcery, or without mana; loot — fire `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(player=p2)` (opponent) → choose_yes_no True + choose_card discards then draws; loot does NOT trigger on controller's own upkeep (`player=p1`). Use the manual `register_triggers` + `fire_event` + `_resolve_stack` (pop/on_resolve/resolve_state_based_actions) convention established in sos_13/sos_120 tests. After sos_201 passes, proceed to task #11 (sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker — read its card_spec.json first), then task #12 (full suite, confirm engine_tests=1145).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/b76fbb6d-7052-44e0-893e-8a2c1cc9d4a6.jsonl\nCon